jt-pve-storage-netapp (0.2.16-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Temp Clone Reaper Idempotency Fix Release
  * Requirements: Proxmox VE 9.1 or later
  * Bug Fix (operational noise, found during v0.2.15 testing):
    - _remove_temp_clone() now detects "volume already absent on ONTAP"
      at entry and returns success, instead of dying at the subsequent
      volume_clone_split call. Previously, a stale tracking entry whose
      ONTAP volume had been deleted out-of-band (interrupted cleanup,
      cross-node race, manual admin action) would cause the TTL
      background reaper to retry every status() poll forever and spam
      the journal with "Failed to cleanup temp clone ...: Volume not
      found" lines. With the fix, the helper returns success on the
      first poll after the issue, the caller untracks the stale entry,
      and the noise stops on the next cycle.
    - Distinguishes confirmed "not found" (volume_get returns undef)
      from transient API errors (volume_get dies) so real failures
      still propagate for retry.

