jt-pve-storage-netapp (0.2.15-1) stable; urgency=high

  * Cross-Storage Orphan Detection Fix Release
  * Requirements: Proxmox VE 9.1 or later
  * Bug Fix (production incident, customer report 2026-05-21..23):
    - _cleanup_orphaned_devices()'s second-pass scan used
      list_netapp_multipath_devices() which returns ALL NETAPP vendor
      multipath devices on the host with no per-storage filter. When
      multiple netappontap storages are configured on the same PVE node
      (e.g. customer with both netappASA and netappFAS_Node2 on the
      same ONTAP cluster -- legitimate setup), each storage's cleanup
      would falsely flag the OTHER storage's healthy LUNs as
      "untracked orphans" and print suggested cleanup commands:
        multipathd disablequeueing map <wwid>
        dmsetup message <wwid> 0 fail_if_no_path
        multipath -f <wwid>
      An operator following those suggestions would tear down active
      VM disks belonging to the sibling storage. Symptom: cluster-wide
      cooldown-rate-limited warnings (one per WWID per hour per node)
      that all referenced perfectly healthy plugin-managed LUNs.
    - Fix: before flagging an untracked NETAPP device as orphan, build
      a union of WWIDs tracked by any OTHER netappontap storage. If
      the device's WWID is found there, skip with no warning -- it
      belongs to a sibling storage and that storage's own cleanup
      handles its own orphans.

