      that mirrors free_image()'s 7-step pattern:
      capture slaves -> unmap -> cleanup_lun_devices -> remove sd* ->
      multipath_reload -> clone_split -> wait -> volume_delete.
  * Operational note:
    - Existing host-side residual devices from backups taken before
      v0.2.14 will NOT be auto-cleaned (plugin design: never auto-clean
      WWIDs not in tracking, to protect customer's manual storage).
      _cleanup_orphaned_devices() will WARN about them via syslog with
      manual cleanup commands. Operators can sweep them with:
        multipath -f <wwid> && echo 1 > /sys/block/sdX/device/delete

