jt-pve-storage-netapp (0.2.13-1) stable; urgency=high

  * Snapshot Delete Cleanup Fix Release
  * Requirements: Proxmox VE 9.1 or later
  * Bug Fix (production incident, customer report 2026-05-13):
    - volume_snapshot_delete() now removes the dependent temp FlexClone
      synchronously before deleting the snapshot. Previous behaviour
      left the cleanup to the TTL-based background task (1 hour),
      so vzdump CT snapshot-mode backups always failed at cleanup
      with "ONTAP job failed: Snapshot copy ... has not expired or
      is locked". The temp FlexClone is created by _get_snapshot_path()
      whenever PVE opens a snapshot for read (vzdump CT backup,
      qm clone --snapname, qemu-img convert, etc.) and locks the
      parent snapshot from deletion. The fix checks for the
      deterministic temp clone name, refuses to proceed if its LUN
      is still in use locally (lsof-style holder check), otherwise
      unmaps + deletes the temp volume, then proceeds with the
      snapshot delete.

