jt-pve-storage-netapp (0.2.12-1) stable; urgency=high

  * iSCSI Portal TCP Pre-check Release
  * Requirements: Proxmox VE 9.1 or later
  * Bug Fixes (sibling-pattern audit from jt-pve-storage-purestorage v1.1.9):
    - activate_storage() now TCP-probes every iSCSI LIF before iscsiadm
      discovery/login. Previous behaviour iterated every portal returned
      by iscsi_get_portals() and called iscsiadm regardless of TCP
      reachability; on multi-LIF SVMs with asymmetric cabling or partial
      fabric reach, every unreachable LIF stalled iscsiadm for 30s
      (discovery) plus up to 60s (login). pvestatd polls activate_storage
      every cycle, so the wedge cascaded into web UI hangs and storage
      starvation. The fix is especially important since v0.2.11 actively
      pushed users toward "distribute LIFs across both controllers", a
      configuration that maximises bug surface when fabric reach is
      asymmetric.
  * API additions:
    - ISCSI::probe_portal($ip, $port, timeout => $t) - bounded
      IO::Socket::INET TCP connect with alarm() guard.
  * New configuration option:
    - ontap-portal-probe-timeout (integer 0..30, default 2). Set to 0 to
      restore pre-0.2.12 behaviour. Raise on high-latency or congested
      storage networks.

