jt-pve-storage-netapp (0.2.0-1) stable; urgency=high

  * Multipath & Migration Fix Release - Anti-Hang Protection
  * Requirements: Proxmox VE 9.1 or later
  * Critical Bug Fixes:
    - Fixed iSCSI multipath only establishing 1 session instead of all portals.
      login_target() checked is_target_logged_in() by IQN only; all ONTAP LIFs
      share the same IQN, so after the first portal login all others were skipped.
      Added is_portal_logged_in() to check portal+target pair individually.
    - Fixed alloc_image() only mapping LUN to current node's igroup in per-node
      mode. Disk migration (move_disk) would hang because the destination node
      could not see the new LUN. Now maps to all node igroups, consistent with
      clone_image() behavior.
  * Anti-Hang Protection (prevents unkillable PVE task workers):
    - Added sysfs_write_with_timeout(): all writes to /sys/ files (SCSI host
      scan, device delete, device rescan, FC issue_lip) now execute in a forked
      child process with 10-second timeout. If the child enters kernel D-state
      due to unresponsive storage, the parent continues instead of hanging.
    - Added sysfs_read_with_timeout(): all reads from /sys/ and /proc/ files
      (device WWID, VPD pages, mount table, FC port attributes) now execute in
      a forked child with 5-second timeout via alarm/pipe.
    - Replaced all bare system() calls with timeout-protected alternatives:
      system('sync') and system('blockdev --flushbufs') now use run_command()
      or _run_cmd() with 10-second timeout in Multipath.pm and Plugin.
    - system('systemctl restart iscsid') now uses _run_cmd() with 30s timeout.
    - system('fuser') in is_device_in_use() now uses _run_cmd() with 10s timeout.
    - glob() calls on /dev/disk/by-id/ now wrapped with alarm(5) timeout.
    - flock(LOCK_EX) on temp clone state file changed to non-blocking LOCK_NB
      with 10-second retry loop to prevent indefinite lock wait.
    - FC.pm _read_file() now uses sysfs_read_with_timeout() for all sysfs reads.
  * Migration Reliability Fixes:
    - Fixed activate_volume() only mapping LUN to current node's igroup. Now
      maps to all node igroups in per-node mode, consistent with alloc_image()
      and clone_image(), preventing device visibility issues during migration.
    - Fixed path() returning synthetic non-existent device path after a single
      failed rescan. Now retries with a proper wait loop (up to ontap-device-timeout,
      default 30s) before falling back to synthetic path, preventing qemu-img
      from failing on newly allocated LUNs that haven't appeared yet.
  * ONTAP Failure Resilience:
    - Reduced API timeout from 30s to 15s and retries from 3 to 2, cutting
      worst-case API call blocking from ~102s to ~34s per call.
    - status() now fails fast if API is unreachable instead of blocking PVE.
    - Temp FlexClone cleanup in status() moved to background fork to prevent
      blocking PVE storage status polling.

